        "text": "<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"shortdescription nomobile noexcerpt noprint searchaux\" style=\"display:none\">Engineering award given by the National Academy of Engineering since 1989</div>\n<p class=\"mw-empty-elt\">\n</p>\n<div class=\"shortdescription nomobile noexcerpt noprint searchaux\" style=\"display:none\">Award</div><style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r1358620234\">@media(min-width:640px){.mw-parser-output .infobox{margin-left:1em;float:right;clear:right;width:22em}}.mw-parser-output .infobox-subbox{padding:0;border:none;margin:-3px;width:auto;min-width:100%;font-size:100%;clear:none;float:none;background-color:transparent;color:inherit}.mw-parser-output .infobox-3cols-child{margin:-3px}.mw-parser-output .infobox .navbar{font-size:100%}.mw-parser-output .infobox-hiddenrow,body.skin--responsive.skin--responsive .mw-parser-output .infobox .infobox-hiddenrow{display:none}@media screen{html.skin-theme-clientpref-night .mw-parser-output .infobox-full-data:not(.notheme)>div:not(.notheme)[style]{background:#1f1f23!important;color:#f8f9fa}}@media screen and (prefers-color-scheme:dark){html.skin-theme-clientpref-os .mw-parser-output .infobox-full-data:not(.notheme)>div:not(.notheme)[style]{background:#1f1f23!important;color:#f8f9fa}}@media(min-width:640px){body.skin--responsive .mw-parser-output .infobox-table{display:table!important}body.skin--responsive .mw-parser-output .infobox-table>caption{display:table-caption!important}body.skin--responsive .mw-parser-output .infobox-table>tbody{display:table-row-group}body.skin--responsive .mw-parser-output .infobox-table th,body.skin--responsive .mw-parser-output .infobox-table td{padding-left:inherit;padding-right:inherit}}</style><table class=\"infobox vevent\"><tbody><tr><th colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-above summary\">Charles Stark Draper Prize</th></tr><tr><td colspan=\"2\" class=\"infobox-image\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File/Frameless\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:Draper-medal.jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/4d/Draper-medal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"198\" height=\"186\" style=\"--mw-file-upright: 1\" class=\"mw-file-element mw-file-upright\" data-file-width=\"198\" data-file-height=\"186\" /></a></span></td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\" class=\"infobox-label\" style=\"width: 33%;\">Presented&#160;by</th><td class=\"infobox-data attendee\"><a href=\"/wiki/National_Academy_of_Engineering\" title=\"National Academy of Engineering\">National Academy of Engineering</a></td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\" class=\"infobox-label\" style=\"width: 33%;\">Reward</th><td class=\"infobox-data\">$500,000</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\" class=\"infobox-label\" style=\"width: 33%;\">First&#160;award</th><td class=\"infobox-data\">1989</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\" class=\"infobox-label\" style=\"width: 33%;\">Website</th><td class=\"infobox-data\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.nae.edu/20681/DraperPrize\">Draper Prize</a></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>The <a href=\"/wiki/National_Academy_of_Engineering\" title=\"National Academy of Engineering\">National Academy of Engineering</a> awards the <b>Charles Stark Draper Prize for Engineering</b>,<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> which is given for the advancement of engineering and the education of the public about engineering. It is one of three prizes that constitute the \"Nobel Prizes of Engineering\"—the others are the Academy's <a href=\"/wiki/Russ_Prize\" title=\"Russ Prize\">Russ</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/Gordon_Prize\" title=\"Gordon Prize\">Gordon Prizes</a>. The Draper Prize is awarded biennially and the winner of each of these prizes receives $500,000.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-2\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup> The Draper Prize is named for <a href=\"/wiki/Charles_Stark_Draper\" title=\"Charles Stark Draper\">Charles Stark Draper</a>, the \"father of <a href=\"/wiki/Inertial_navigation\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Inertial navigation\">inertial navigation</a>\", an <a href=\"/wiki/MIT\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"MIT\">MIT</a> professor and founder of <a href=\"/wiki/Charles_Stark_Draper_Laboratory\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Charles Stark Draper Laboratory\">Draper Laboratory</a>.\n</p>\n<div class=\"mw-references-wrap\"><ol class=\"references\">\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-1\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-1\">^</a></b></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.nae.edu/20681.aspx\">Charles Stark Draper Prize – Home</a></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-2\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-2\">^</a></b></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.nae.edu/20681/DraperPrize\">Charles Stark Draper Prize – Awards</a></span>\n</li>\n</ol></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nParsed by mw‐api‐ext.eqiad.main‐77f8cc8f9b‐kk98k\nCached time: 20260918181054\nCache expiry: 2592000\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [vary‐revision‐sha1]\nCPU time usage: 0.085 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.144 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 1119/1000000\nRevision size: 1205/2097152 bytes\nPost‐expand include size: 6803/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 1471/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 12/100\nExpensive parser function count: 1/500\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 1735/5000000 bytes\nLua time usage: 0.046/10.000 seconds\nLua memory usage: 3382962/52428800 bytes\nNumber of Wikibase entities loade